{"name":"Delicate Lilac Crystal","hex":"#d7d2e2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"delicate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily damaged or requiring careful handling.","Characterized by a fine structure or thin lines."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A delicate item of clothing, especially underwear or lingerie.","A choice dainty; a delicacy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate"},{"term":"lilac","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large shrub of the genus Syringa, especially Syringa vulgaris, bearing white, pale-pink, or purple flowers.","A flower of the lilac shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Of a cat or its fur: having a pale brown colour, lighter than chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lilac"},{"term":"crystal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid composed of an array of atoms or molecules possessing long-range order and arranged in a pattern which is periodic in three dimensions.","A piece of glimmering, shining mineral resembling ice or glass."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of crystal.","Very clear; coherent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crystal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Syringa","blocks":[{"text":"Syringa is a genus of 12 currently recognized species of flowering woody plants in the olive family known colloquially as lilacs. They are native to woodland and scrub from southeastern Europe to eastern Asia, and widely and commonly cultivated in temperate areas elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syringa","wikidata":"Q157449"},{"title":"Crystal","blocks":[{"text":"A crystal or crystalline solid is a solid material whose constituents are arranged in a highly ordered microscopic structure, forming a crystal lattice that extends in all directions. In addition, macroscopic single crystals are usually identifiable by their geometrical shape, consisting of flat faces with specific, characteristic orientations. The scientific study of crystals and crystal formation is known as crystallography. The process of crystal formation via mechanisms of crystal growth is called crystallization or solidification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Quartz_28.jpg/330px-Quartz_28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal","wikidata":"Q43533"},{"title":"Lilac (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lilac is a light shade of purple or violet representing the average color of most lilac flowers. The colors of some lilac flowers may be equivalent to the colors shown below as pale lilac, rich lilac, or deep lilac. However, there are other lilac flowers that are colored red-violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilac_(color)","wikidata":"Q12894641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/500px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/1280px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/500px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Purple lilac bush","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALilac_Bush.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Lilac_buds.jpg/500px-Lilac_buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi